Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — markup with `@typeparam TItem`, a `@key`'d loop rendering each item's template plus Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — code-behind `partial class`:
- Copies the incoming `Items` parameter to a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the original).
- `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` swap items in the internal list, then invoke `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the new order.

Usage matches your example — just note `OnOrderChanged` delivers an `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`:

```csharp
private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
{
    tasks = newOrder.ToList();
}
```
